 an e-commerce platform, with various conditions and filters applied to the data.\n\nThe query can be rewritten using the provided rewrite rule, which suggests replacing certain logical operations with more efficient ones. For example, some of the join conditions can be replaced with more specific joins, and some of the filter conditions can be combined or simplified.\n\nHere is a possible rewritten version of the SQL query:\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n  channel,\n  id,\n  SUM(sales) AS sales,\n  SUM(returns) AS returns,\n  SUM(profit) AS profit\nFROM (\n  SELECT \n    'web channel' AS channel,\n    'web_site' AS id,\n    ws_ext_sales_price AS sales,\n    wr_return_amt AS returns,\n    -ws_net_profit AS profit\n  FROM web_sales WS\n  JOIN web_returns WR ON WS.ws_item_sk = WR.wr_item_sk AND WS.ws_order_number = WR.wr_order_number\n  WHERE \n    WS.ws_sold_date_sk = D.date_sk\n    AND D.d_date >= '1999-09-30'\n    AND D.d_date <= DATE_ADD('1999-09-30', INTERVAL 30 DAY)\n    AND WS.ws_web_site_sk = W.web_site_sk\n    AND WS.ws_item_sk = I.i_item_sk\n    AND I.i_current_price > 50\n    AND (I.i_category IN ('Books', 'Electronics') OR WS.ws_promo_sk = P.promo_sk)\n    AND (P.p_channel_email = 'Y' AND P.p_channel_tv = 'Y' AND P.p_channel_radio = 'N' AND P.p_channel_press = 'Y' AND P.p_channel_event = 'Y')\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT \n    'catalog channel' AS channel,\n    'catalog_page' AS id,\n    cs_ext_sales_price AS sales,\n    cr_return_amount AS returns,\n    -cs_net_profit AS profit\n  FROM catalog_sales CS\n  JOIN catalog_returns CR ON CS.cs_item_sk = CR.cr_item_sk AND CS.cs_order_number = CR.cr_order_number\n  WHERE \n    CS.cs_sold_date_sk = D.date_sk\n    AND D.d_date >= '1999-09-30'\n    AND D.d_date <= DATE_ADD('1999-09-30', INTERVAL 30 DAY)\n    AND CS.cs_catalog_page_sk = CP.catalog_page_sk\n    AND CS.cs_item_sk = I.i_item_sk\n    AND I.i_current_price > 50\n    AND (I.i_category IN ('Books', 'Electronics') OR CS.cs_promo_sk = P.promo_sk)\n    AND (P.p_channel_email = 'Y' AND P.p_channel_tv = 'Y' AND P.p_channel_radio = 'N' AND P.p_channel_press = 'Y' AND P.p_channel_event = 'Y')\n) AS subquery\nGROUP BY channel, id;\n```\n\nThis rewritten query uses a UNION ALL operator to combine the results from two separate queries, one for web sales and one for catalog sales. The filter conditions have been simplified and combined where possible, and some of the joins have been replaced with more specific ones.", 'time': 14.066926956176758}
